    "analysis": "This is a mirror/fork of kevinwatt/yt-dlp-mcp, a Model Context Protocol server that wraps yt-dlp to give LLMs YouTube capabilities: listing and downloading subtitles in SRT format, and downloading videos at a chosen resolution to the user's Downloads folder. It's a small Node.js/TypeScript MCP server intended for use with MCP-compatible LLM clients such as Dive Desktop, installed via `npx`. Aimed at developers wiring YouTube content access into an AI agent without exposing tracking-based download paths.",
